{
  "name": "memory-contradictions",
  "version": 3,
  "description": "Human-labeled contradiction cases for the deterministic conflict detector. Each case states one existing active memory, one new statement, the new statement's authority, and the SAFE expected disposition. Kinds: direct-polarity, paraphrase-conflict, confirmation, unrelated, different-subject, different-scope, temporary, observation-vs-preference, replacement, ambiguous, authority, numeric-value, negation, subject-alias, temporal. A missed conflict is safer than a false conflict, so unrelated/scope/subject cases expect 'none'. v3 repurposes the retired semantic layer's value-substitution and paraphrase safety cases as LEXICAL regression cases (kind numeric-value/paraphrase-conflict): they guard the previously-shipped bug where a changed value was silently confirmed. The optional semantic candidate layer was removed on the evidence that deterministic normalization closed the measured gap.",
